## Key points

1. The Bank will buy the asset from the seller and own it before leasing it to you. Until then there is no lease.
2. Rent starts only when the asset is delivered to you and you sign the delivery and acceptance certificate.
3. While the Bank owns the asset it bears the risks of ownership, including takaful on the asset and major structural maintenance. You are responsible for ordinary use and routine maintenance.
4. Ownership transfers to you at the end of the term under a separate promise to transfer, once all rentals are paid.
5. If you pay late, any late-payment amount charged is paid to charity. It is not income of the Bank.

To accept, sign the Promise to Lease that accompanies this letter.
